<exercise class="RFM1">
  <problem>
    <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
    
    <para>Kiran says we should add the constraint \( t ≥ 0 \).</para>
    
    <para>What is the reasoning behind this constraint?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>We can't have a negative ticket price.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--End interaction-->

<!--Q#2-->
<exercise class="RFM1">
  <problem>
    <para>What other “natural constraint” like this should be added?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>By the same reasoning, we might want to include \(m \geq 0\). Note that the other variables should also be greater than or equal to 0, but those conditions are already implied by the existing constraints.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--End interaction-->
</section>
